   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>manipulatr-ers,</div><div><br></div><div>Within a function, I&#39;m trying to exclude rows with NAs in one column using dplyr::filter, but leave in rows that may have NAs in other columns (therefore, I can&#39;t pipe the data frame through na.omit). The column name is given by the user of the function. Here&#39;s a toy example:</div><div><br></div><div>library(&quot;dplyr&quot;)</div><div>library(&quot;lazyeval&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>df &lt;- data_frame(</div><div>  dept = c(&quot;marketing&quot;, &quot;marketing&quot;, &quot;marketing&quot;, &quot;accounting&quot;, &quot;accounting&quot;),</div><div>  person = c(&quot;Bob&quot;, &quot;Bill&quot;, &quot;Rich&quot;, &quot;Stan&quot;, &quot;Fred&quot;),</div><div>  age = c(23, 34, NA, 45, NA),</div><div>  salary = c(8000, NA, 10000, NA, 20000)</div><div>)</div><div><br></div><div>## begin function definition ##</div><div>get_info &lt;- function(<a href=\"http://df.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://df.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0OhWBTAp_9f7IBtzfC_FjB\">df.name</a>, <a href=\"http://dept.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dept.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NMVpq03QzMk0RgI4TigcK\">dept.name</a>, <a href=\"http://col.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://col.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c46WpRTrQI4XtJtjoF1Rx\">col.name</a>) {    </div><div>  output &lt;- </div><div>    <a href=\"http://df.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://df.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0OhWBTAp_9f7IBtzfC_FjB\">df.name</a> %&gt;%</div><div>    filter(dept == <a href=\"http://dept.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dept.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NMVpq03QzMk0RgI4TigcK\">dept.name</a>) %&gt;%</div><div>    </div><div>    # TRYING TO EXCLUDE NAs IN THE COLUMN SPECIFIED BY THE USER</div><div>    filter(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LwqAB3AhUkQWTLkLzrkMH\">is.na</a>(<a href=\"http://col.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://col.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c46WpRTrQI4XtJtjoF1Rx\">col.name</a>))</div><div>#     filter_(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LwqAB3AhUkQWTLkLzrkMH\">is.na</a>(~<a href=\"http://col.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://col.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c46WpRTrQI4XtJtjoF1Rx\">col.name</a>))</div><div>#     filter_(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LwqAB3AhUkQWTLkLzrkMH\">is.na</a>(interp(quote(<a href=\"http://var.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://var.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FMwuD5GsdUU3LgVXtad9Y\">var.name</a>), <a href=\"http://var.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://var.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FMwuD5GsdUU3LgVXtad9Y\">var.name</a> = <a href=\"http://col.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://col.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c46WpRTrQI4XtJtjoF1Rx\">col.name</a>)))</div><div>#     filter_(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LwqAB3AhUkQWTLkLzrkMH\">is.na</a>(~interp(<a href=\"http://col.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://col.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c46WpRTrQI4XtJtjoF1Rx\">col.name</a>)))  </div><div>#     filter_(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LwqAB3AhUkQWTLkLzrkMH\">is.na</a>(~interp(<a href=\"http://var.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://var.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FMwuD5GsdUU3LgVXtad9Y\">var.name</a>, <a href=\"http://var.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://var.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FMwuD5GsdUU3LgVXtad9Y\">var.name</a> = <a href=\"http://col.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://col.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357615520000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c46WpRTrQI4XtJtjoF1Rx\">col.name</a>)))</div><div>  </div><div>  return(output)</div><div>} </div><div>## end function definition ##</div><div><br></div><div># tests the function</div><div>get_info(df, &quot;marketing&quot;, &quot;age&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>This returns:</div><div>       dept person age salary</div><div>1 marketing    Bob  23   8000</div><div>2 marketing   Bill  34     NA</div><div>3 marketing   Rich  NA  10000</div><div><br></div><div>Rather than the desired:</div><div>       dept person age salary</div><div>1 marketing    Bob  23   8000</div><div>2 marketing   Bill  34     NA</div><div><br></div><div>My attempts with the SE version filter_() are commented out so you can see what I&#39;ve tried.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for any words of wisdom with this.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>If important, here&#39;s my sessionInfo():</div><div><br></div><div><div>R version 3.2.0 (2015-04-16)</div><div>Platform: x86_64-apple-darwin13.4.0 (64-bit)</div><div>Running under: OS X 10.10.3 (Yosemite)</div><div><br></div><div>locale:</div><div>[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8</div><div><br></div><div>attached base packages:</div><div>[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     </div><div><br></div><div>other attached packages:</div><div>[1] lazyeval_0.1.10 dplyr_0.4.1    </div><div><br></div><div>loaded via a namespace (and not attached):</div><div>[1] magrittr_1.5   assertthat_0.1 parallel_3.2.0 DBI_0.3.1      tools_3.2.0    Rcpp_0.11.5   </div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
